      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to find the smallest possible value of \\( n \\) (the number of steps in the flight of stairs) that satisfies the following conditions:\n1. \\( n \\equiv 3 \\pmod{4} \\)\n2. \\( n \\equiv 2 \\pmod{5} \\)\n3. \\( n > 10 \\)\n\nWe can start by iterating through the values of \\( n \\) that satisfy the first two conditions and checking if they are greater than 10. Let's implement this in Python:\n\n```python\n# Iterate through values of n to find the smallest possible value that satisfies the conditions\nfor n in range(11, 100):  # starting from 11 because n > 10\n    if n % 4 == 3 and n % 5 == 2:\n        smallest_n = n\n        break\n\nprint(smallest_n)\n```\n```output\n12\n```\nThe smallest possible value of \\( n \\) that satisfies the given conditions is \\(\\boxed{23}\\).",
